From 9fc21a43604b6a7cac3ccb6cb2b95d064f38e062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:21:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] feat(api): derive the decision risk level on the server

The decisions endpoint never passed a risk level, so every request ran
with the internal default "low" and the router's high-risk protection
(refuse without a fallback provider, never adopt a fallback candidate
automatically) could not trigger through the API.

The server now derives the level from the operation domain, the part of
`question` before the first dot: the domains of the high-risk operations
listed in architecture 14.2 (driver, node, mig, gpu, device, plugin,
model, quota, tenant, policy, system, platform) are high, inference is
low, anything else is medium. A client may raise the level with
riskLevel but never lower it. The effective level is returned in the
response and in the error details.

A FALLBACK_REQUIRED result used to fall into DECISION_NO_CANDIDATE with
a misleading "no provider returned a valid candidate" message; it now
returns 503 DECISION_FALLBACK_REQUIRED with the candidates in the
details for manual approval, still without adopting any of them. The
OpenAPI document gains riskLevel, the derivation rule and the 503
outcomes, and no longer marks context as required, since the server
defaults it.
